    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d858">

                <pb facs="0933" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/137</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-24T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3357. Your 4335, May 20, 2 p. m. I am pleased to learn that you have succeeded so
                    well in obtaining the release of all of the persons seized from the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">China</hi> with the full admission of the principle for
                    which the United States has always stood.</p>
                <p>At an opportune time, but without such delay as would indicate lack of interest
                    on my part, please press for the release of the men in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Henry S.</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Ausable</hi>
                    cases. The German Ambassador formally informs me that neither of the men taken
                    from the <hi rendition="#italic">Henry S.</hi> were members of the armed forces
                    of Germany, Austria-Hungary or Turkey, but that they were simply civilians in
                    the private American sea service, without any German connection whatever.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
